   la djan e la meris cu tcidu le vo'a cukta
   le re prenu cu tcidu le vo'a cukta

i.e., when a prosumti refers to several things not massified,
how do we interpret it? Is the first one:

   la djan tcidu le vo'a cukta ije
   la meris tcidu le vo'a cukta

or is it:

   la djan tcidu le cukta pe la djan e la meris ije
   la meris tcidu le cukta pe la djan e la meris

?

It doesn't make sense to worry about how to say "respectively"
before we know what the basic case means. Maybe it already
means "respectively" on its own. That's my preference.

